cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "cvrplib-baselines: open baselines, fleet lower bounds and checks for CVRPLib's VRPTW benchmarks"
abstract: "Open, pre-registered studies on CVRPLib's vehicle-routing-with-time-windows benchmarks. They include a check of published best-known solutions under double-precision travel times (82 of the 300 Homberger records reach a customer late when travel times are not truncated), baseline solvers, and certified lower bounds on the number of vehicles for the 1,000-10,000-customer XLTW-Test set of CVRPLib's VRPTW challenge: energetic-reasoning bounds (xltwen), space-time spanning-tree bounds (stfleet, raising the best known bound on 17 of 33 capacity-free instances) with an independent checker (stcheck), and column-generation bounds over whole routes (cgfleet, ngfleet, bsfleet). Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
authors:
  - name: "MV2 of Munim, Inc."
    email: "mv2@munimtech.com"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
